  <title>7.16.3: Quadratic Equations and Graphs</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02030</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.16.3: Quadratic Equations and Graphs</md:title>
    <md:uuid>a1ac3380-f6ca-422f-bf1f-e44847722882</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <para>
        <figure>
          <media alt="GRAPHS A THROUGH F. GRAPH A IS A PARABOLA THAT OPENS UP WITH A VERTEX AT (4, 1). GRAPH B IS A PARABOLA THAT OPENS UP WITH A VERTEX AT (NEGATIVE 1, NEGATIVE 4). GRAPH C IS A PARABOLA THAT OPENS DOWN WITH A VERTEX AT (4, 1). GRAPH D IS A PARABOLA THAT OPENS DOWN WITH A VERTEX AT (NEGATIVE 1, NEGATIVE 4). GRAPH E IS A PARABOLA THAT OPENS UP WITH A VERTEX AT (NEGATIVE 4, NEGATIVE 1). GRAPH F IS A PARABOLA THAT OPENS UP WITH A VERTEX AT (1, 4).">
            <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_18_06_01.png"/>
          </media>
        </figure>
        <link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/f38d59f200df6a983128aa7f5619f7153bdd8c78">Moodle 6.16.3 Image of all 6 graphs</link>
      </para>
      <para>Your teacher will give you a <link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/731925b6969bc490346728eef9715f3856fc95f1">set of cards</link>. Each card contains an equation or a graph that represents a quadratic function. Take turns matching each equation to a graph that represents the same function.</para>
      <list>
        <item> For each pair of cards that you match, explain to your partner how you know they belong together. </item>
        <item> For each pair of cards that your partner matches, listen carefully to their explanation. If you disagree, discuss your thinking and work to reach an agreement. </item>
        <item> Once all the cards are matched, record the equation, the letter of the equation, and a sketch of the corresponding graph, and write a brief note or explanation about how you knew they were a match. </item>
      </list>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <title>Activity</title>
        <exercise id="a5a39f83-9dbe-449a-a961-b24d10d83459" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <newline/>
            <para>Choose the equation that matches this graph.</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(f(x)=(x−1)^2+4\)</para>
            <para>\(g(x)=-(x−4)^2+1\)</para>
            <para>\(h(x)=(x+1)^2−4\) </para>
            <para>\(p(x)=-(x+1)^2−4\)</para>
            <para>\(q(x)=2(x−4)^2+1\)</para>
            <para>\(r(x)=(x+4)^2−1\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(f(x)=(x−1)^2+4\)</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(f(x)=(x−1)^2+4\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
